{"title":"2013 MPFG Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_MPFG_Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let f be the function defined by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/8/2a80bb3f2939ab5b919446213b5528f22fc352c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = -2 sin(\\pi x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"20\" /> . How many values of x such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/1/fa135d67da7922fa6488bad467e56c032c76fbb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2 \\leq x \\leq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" /> satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/d/ebd442b287ac55e7cf4df234f650225a644c42a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(f(x))) = f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_MPFG_Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We first create the graph of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> by transforming a regular <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/8/428cdedd4ee7d20c333788c082439c332f706b37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$sin$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" /> graph by scaling down <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> and scaling up <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/a/62a76677add1d246708c86edfc7c4b8a40184914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Graph_of_f(x).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/01/Graph_of_f%28x%29.jpg/400px-Graph_of_f%28x%29.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"398\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/01/Graph_of_f%28x%29.jpg/600px-Graph_of_f%28x%29.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/01/Graph_of_f%28x%29.jpg/800px-Graph_of_f%28x%29.jpg 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>We observe that the domain &amp; range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> is restricted in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60010fd01c6801d1b857f1acefb200f1ee8c682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-2,2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" /> and the graph is restricted in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad0e2f0d4d7cf8de454cebcdf2fed5fa0e5afff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> square. Trying out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d605a9093a45ef214a0cf1a7c0829e16363c07d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />, we see that every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c339afa03e060d959e4942be7522c0c992f4c41c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> of a cycle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> ranges over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b7dad4fb35e4c2f4d7b9c767ddb8709ebf2446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,\\pm 2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" />, which means a cycle for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/2/832412dadeda9dcad97d7701cf955690a5827c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"20\" /> will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> cycles for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d605a9093a45ef214a0cf1a7c0829e16363c07d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d605a9093a45ef214a0cf1a7c0829e16363c07d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" /> have two crossing points in each small cycle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/0/d605a9093a45ef214a0cf1a7c0829e16363c07d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-center\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Graph_of_f(f(x)).jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0b/Graph_of_f%28f%28x%29%29.jpg/400px-Graph_of_f%28f%28x%29%29.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"402\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0b/Graph_of_f%28f%28x%29%29.jpg/600px-Graph_of_f%28f%28x%29%29.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/0/0b/Graph_of_f%28f%28x%29%29.jpg/800px-Graph_of_f%28f%28x%29%29.jpg 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>As such, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/8/788d684e6bbaca824ca4e6bdbe71295684949b5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(f(x))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> will have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f4a16732c81c26b2767a596a3d7a9006d72761.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot4^{2} = 32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" /> cycles in the domain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/0/f60010fd01c6801d1b857f1acefb200f1ee8c682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[-2,2]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"48\" height=\"18\" />. Each has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points that cross with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/6/c96dd6ec1dc4ad7520fbdc78fcdbec9edd068d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"37\" height=\"20\" />. However, at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> special locations, the crossing points of two consecutive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c50ee41c8bccf34cfb334c37a7a072bc15b0c40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(f(x)))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" /> cycles overlapped (at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/9/ba986e04b154275a28bee01a468a56739e9954b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=-1, 0, 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"94\" height=\"17\" />).\nAs such, number of total points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/d/e6d8d76a8164d2c3c7b900bcf8934ec402aa3514.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\cdot32-3 = \\boxed{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"127\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>～cassphe\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018055845\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.064 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 104/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5440/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:33485:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018055845 and revision id 258510. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}